build/
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
*.wav
ext/synth1/
# The CLAP headers are a separate upstream checkout (its own git repository),
# read as the reference for src/clap. Nothing in the build consumes them: the
# bindings are pure Odin, so the headers are not vendored here.
ext/clap/
Synth1V113beta3.zip
# Workflow scratch, not part of the project.
.atomic/

# Runtime state of the editor tooling. `.claude/launch.json` is deliberately not
# ignored -- it is the shared dev-server definition and belongs to the project.
.claude/*.lock
ext/vst3_c_api/

# The WebView2 header is 2.5 MB of generated COM declarations, read as the
# reference for src/webview2 the same way ext/clap and ext/vst3_c_api are read
# for their bindings -- and ignored for the same reason: nothing in the build
# consumes it, the bindings are pure Odin. ext/webview2/README.md says which
# package to fetch it from.
#
# WebView2Loader.dll beside it is deliberately *not* ignored. That one is a real
# runtime dependency: tools/install-vst3.ps1 copies it into the bundle, and a
# fresh checkout could not build a working editor without it.
ext/webview2/include/

# Synth1's own factory banks, shipped with the reference and copied here to be
# measured against. They are not this project's work and not ours to
# redistribute, so they stay on disk and out of the history -- the null test and
# tools/uibank read them from the working tree and neither needs them committed.
# Written as `patches/*` with an exception rather than `patches/`, because git
# does not descend into an ignored directory, so a negation under a directory
# ignored as a whole would never be reached. patches/quesynth is this project's
# own bank and is committed; the rest is Synth1's.
patches/*
!patches/quesynth/

# Third-party Synth1 patch banks, by their own authors. Downloaded to test
# against, and no more ours to redistribute than the factory banks above.
zipbank.zip
zipbank/

# Synth1's own manual. Read as the primary source for the reference's documented
# behaviour -- docs/reference-notes.md says where to get it -- but it carries its
# author's copyright and is no more ours to ship than the binary it documents.
docs/synth1-readme-eng.txt

# The WebAssembly engine is a build artifact; CI builds it for the page.
hosts/wasm/synth.wasm

# The bank the interface reads is generated, not written.
#
# `patches/quesynth/factory.json` is the source and is committed; this is a
# transcription of it into the form the panel can load with no fetch and no
# parser. Committing both would be committing the same bank twice, and the copy
# would be the one that goes stale.
#
# Everything that ships the panel generates it first -- the Pages workflow, the
# release workflow and tools/install-vst3.ps1 all run tools/uibank -- so a
# checkout without this file is not missing anything it cannot rebuild:
#     odin run tools/uibank
ui/bank.js

# Browser QA scratch: snapshots, console logs and videos from the Playwright
# CLI, written beside whatever was being checked. Evidence for one session, not
# a record of anything measured.
.playwright-cli/

research/